window.STUDY={"id":"ap-38-all-day-poster-type-printed","code":"AP-38","title":"All-day poster · type, printed","fig":"4.38","kicker":"Application · 38","lede":"The all-day poster's type on its own: every dial changes how the letters print and nothing else.","body":["The headline, the bill and the rules are inked by the same chain as the block; Face sets how the letters take ink, Edge works their edges and outline. The ember block and the press bar are printed at AP-37's defaults and do not move."],"source":"Split from AP-07 (All-day poster · the ink runs out with the day) into two instruments: this type page and AP-37, which holds the roller. Made with the effect set.","ref":{"w":1500,"h":2250},"variants":[{"id":"set","label":"As drawn","sw":[]}],"points":[],"colorHint":"The inks are the card's own: the brand ink on the wordmark, black on the key.","paramsHint":"Face and edge: only the type answers.","spec":{"usage":{"id":"u-allday-type","job":"print","title":"All-day poster · type, printed","aspect":"2/3","uses":["fx-02-ink-edge","type-edge"],"split_of":"u-allday","role":"type"},"reference":{"grammar":"The all-day poster's type on its own: every dial changes how the letters print and nothing else. The headline, the bill and the rules are inked by the same chain as the block; Face sets how the letters take ink, Edge works their edges and outline. The ember block and the press bar are printed at AP-37's defaults and do not move."},"techniques":[{"id":"fx-02-ink-edge","name":"Face","short":"FX-02","atoms":["deposit"],"params":{"imp":{"value":0.985,"range":[0.78,1],"label":"Impression","step":0.005,"note":"how hard the forme meets the board. Below 1 the letters open onto the board's valleys: a kiss impression"},"starve":{"value":0.012,"range":[0,0.2],"label":"Starve","step":0.002,"scale":"pow","curve":2,"note":"the lowest share of the board inside each letter never takes ink: pinholes"},"mottle":{"value":0.2,"range":[0,0.6],"label":"Mottle","step":0.01,"note":"the sheet's formation thinning the film inside the letters. Past .6 the clouds read as blotches"},"density":{"value":1.35,"range":[0.8,1.8],"label":"Film thickness","step":0.01,"note":"ink film on the letters. The wordmark's brand ink and the black key thin and deepen together"}},"implementation":"The letters are inked by the same chain as the roll: the board under each letter is ranked to percentiles and the impression inks its top share, so a light impression opens the face onto the valleys, starve pins the lowest share and the formation mottles the film. The letter's own edge is the coverage, worked in Edge.","limits":"Impression < .78: the face falls apart into speckle and the small setting stops reading."},{"id":"type-edge","name":"Edge","short":"Type","atoms":["deposit"],"params":{"spread":{"value":0.12,"range":[-0.45,0.9],"label":"Ink spread","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"film squeezed past the letter's edge (+), or the edge eaten back by a starved forme (−). Full on display letters, less on small type, where counters close and hairlines vanish first"},"rag":{"value":0.32,"range":[0,1],"label":"Edge rag","step":0.01,"unit":"px","scale":"pow","curve":2,"note":"how far the board's tooth pushes the edge in and out, half as far on small type. 0 is a cut vector edge"},"wander":{"value":0.3,"range":[0,1.6],"label":"Edge wander","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"a slow waver along the edge: a soft roller, a worn forme. Full on display letters, an eighth of it on small type"},"wScale":{"value":22,"range":[4,80],"label":"Wander scale","step":0.5,"unit":"px","scale":"log","note":"wavelength of the waver"},"feather":{"value":0.3,"range":[0,1.6],"label":"Feather","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"how far ink wicks past the edge along the paper's grain, in hairlines; about half as far on small type. Past 1.6 px it reads as fuzz"},"ebite":{"value":0,"range":[0,1],"label":"Edge bite","step":0.01,"note":"clumped dropouts that grow likelier toward the edge: worn wood type. Display letters take it in full, small type barely"},"rim":{"value":1.2,"range":[0.4,6],"label":"Rim width","step":0.05,"unit":"px","scale":"log","note":"the band along each edge where the squeezed film sits at full strength"},"face":{"value":0.88,"range":[0,1],"label":"Face ink","step":0.01,"note":"film in the face against the rim. 1 is an even solid; lower leaves a darker rim, the letterpress squash; 0 prints only the rim: outline type"},"contour":{"value":0,"range":[0,1.6],"label":"Contour line","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"a line around each display letter, set off by a gap that grows with it; small type is left alone. 0 is none"},"seed":{"value":7,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"a new forme: the same settings, a different wander and bite"}},"implementation":"Each letter's alpha becomes a signed distance in device px. The edge is moved by spread, pushed by the board's height (rag), waved by noise (wander), eaten near the edge (bite) and feathered along fibers; the rim keeps full film while the face thins (face 0 = outline type), and a contour hairline sits off the edge. Coverage stays one device px wide, so the edge is crisp at any setting.","limits":"Ink spread > .9 px closes the counters of the small mono labels. Edge rag > 1 px reads as a fuzz filter. Wander, bite and the contour scale with the letter: on small type they would break the setting."}],"pass_order":["Face · how the letters take ink from the forme.","Edge · spread, rag, wander, feather and bite at the edge; the squeezed rim, outline and contour."]}};
